Navigation note: the web route /period-compare is single-segment, so the first-segment AppRouteParser resolves it directly
via the new route's pathSegment ("period-compare") — and the two web redirects (App.tsx: /compare and /analytics/compare
-> /period-compare) are added to AppRouteParser.aliases, mirroring the existing /statistics -> .analytics alias. A dedicated
.periodCompare route (Insights sidebar group) was added rather than displacing the existing .analytics (= Statistics) or
.fleetCompare routes (covenant #7). The pathSegment is unique (testEveryRouteHasUniquePathSegment stays green); the route
resolves to its Insights group (testEveryRouteResolvesToItsGroup stays green). The web "Open Fleet comparison" banner CTA
navigates through an injected onNavigate shell hook (selection = .fleetCompare), mirroring FleetCompareRouteRegistration;
the banner dismissal persists in UserDefaults under the web localStorage key phase40.compareBanner.dismissed.period.

